# 2026-10-08-struct-operator-results.md, item 6 (lane E2's q/c1.cyr): a write to a captured NAME inside
# a closure is reported as "undefined variable 'x'" though `x` is defined, captured and readable in
# the same body (`|d| { return x + d; }` builds and returns 7). Run from the repo root (includes).
# Expected: a diagnostic that names the real refusal (a captured name is not assignable in the
# closure). Actual: error:<source>:11:25: undefined variable 'x'
include "lib/syscalls.cyr"
include "lib/alloc.cyr"
include "lib/fnptr.cyr"
fn main(): i64 {
    var x = 5;
    var f = |d| { x += d; return x; };
    return callptr(f, 2);
}
syscall(60, main());
